DESCRIPTION:Language Exchange Toronto - Se Habla English & Spanish\n**Span
 ish Language Conversation Toronto** is part of ***Se Habla.***\n\n“Se Ha
 bla” is a leading online community for cultural and linguistic exchange 
 where you can participate in enriching sessions\, make new friends\, and c
 onnect with a growing global network. With 9 Meetup groups across 9 cities
  in 6 countries\, Se Habla is truly open to everyone from Alaska to Patago
 nia\, and from Europe and Asia to Australia. Join us and don’t miss the 
 opportunity to practice with native speakers.\n\n**We have been meeting si
 nce June 2020 on the following days:**\n\n* Monday\n* Wednesday\n* Sunday\
 n\nWith a one-time donation\, you can join the meetings as many times as y
 ou like and stay as long as you wish.\n\n**Format**\n**Conversation Rooms 
 (Everyday and All levels)**\nDepending on attendance and nationality\, sma
 ll groups are formed with 4-6 people:\n\n* 2 native English speakers\n* 2 
 native Spanish speakers\n* 1 native speaker of another language\n\nThe mee
 tings last for 2 hours and are divided into 4 periods:\n\n* 30 minutes spe
 aking in English\n* 30 minutes speaking in Spanish\n* 30 minutes speaking 
 in English\n* 30 minutes speaking in Spanish\n\n**Beginner Room (Optional 
 and only Mondays)**\nWelcome\, English and Spanish beginners.\n**Check the
  English and Spanish lessons** **here »** [https://myspanishclass.xyz/](h
 ttps://myspanishclass.xyz/)\n\n**Debate Room (Optional and only Wednesday)
 **\nNew topic each week.\n**Check the discussion topics here »** [https:/
 /se-habla.com/category/article/](https://se-habla.com/category/article/)\n
 \nPlease note that **we speak half of the time in English and half in Span
 ish.** We help each other learn both languages.\n\n**After two hours**\, e
 veryone returns to the main room to meet all participants and take a group
  screenshot. If you have time\, you’re welcome to stay and continue the 
 conversation for as long as you like.\n\n**Community**\n**We have 9 MeetUp
  groups meeting at the same time** (Mexico City\, Calgary\, Vancouver\, To
 ronto\, New York\, London\, Los Angeles\, Medellín\, and Santiago de Chil
 e). However\, during the exchange\, you will meet people not only from the
 se cities but also from all over the world.\n\nYou can get the link to our
  9 MeetUp groups by visiting any of the following pages:\n[https://se-habl
 a.com/spanish-meetup/](https://se-habla.com/spanish-meetup/)\n[[https://se
 -habla.com/english-meetup/](https://se-habla.com/english-meetup/)\n\n**One
 -Time Donation**\nFor over four years\, the meetings were free\, but curre
 ntly I am requesting a **ONE-TIME DONATION** to access the meetings and he
 lp to cover the costs of the 9 MeetUp Groups and Zoom.\n\nYou can make the
  one-time donation at the link below. Afterward\, PayPal will redirect you
  to a page where you'll find the Zoom link to join the meeting.\n[https://
 se-habla.com/language-exchange](https://se-habla.com/language-exchange/)\n
 \nIf you have already donated and don't have the Zoom link\, please contac
 t me.\n\n**Please don’t hesitate to reach out if you have any further qu
 estions.**\n\nSee you soon\,\nHéctor Fuentes
